    "abstract": "With public debt high across Europe, how fiscal consolidations affect productivity is again a live question. This column studies spending-based consolidations in 139 euro area regions between 1999 and 2019, using a new utilisation-adjusted measure of total factor productivity. In regions more exposed to consolidation, output falls while measured productivity rises. The productivity gains arise almost entirely within sectors and coincide with a net decline in business establishments.",
