  {
    "abstract": "Can environmental certification improve environmental performance beyond certified firms? Using China’s Green Factory certification as the empirical setting, we examine whether government-backed voluntary environmental certification generates environmental benefits along supply chains. Exploiting the staggered certification of core firms and supply-chain links among Chinese A-share listed firms from 2009 to 2023, we find that certification improves the environmental performance of suppliers and customers by about 4.17%. Mechanism evidence points to strengthened supply-chain bargaining power and relationship-based green technology spillovers as two important channels. The effect is larger for suppliers, highly dependent partners, firms in heavily polluting industries, and firms with environmentally experienced executives. The findings suggest that green certification can do more than reward leading firms: if credibly designed and continuously monitored, it can help diffuse cleaner production practices across supply chains.",
